#---
# purpose: "Enum tier-0 functions return Elixir-style public values across List, Range, and Map"
# oracle: oracle.exs
# timeout.interp_secs: 15
# timeout.run_secs: 15
#---
#
# Exercises the reduce-based public `Enum` surface that later Enum functions build
# on: `reduce/2`, `reduce/3`, `reduce_while/3`, `each/2`, `count/1`, `count/2`,
# `member?/2`, `to_list/1`, and `reverse/1,2`. The reduce family runs over List,
# Range, and Map so the "across List, Range, and Map" claim is exercised, not just
# asserted.
#
# `Enum.reduce/2` -- the no-accumulator form -- seeds the fold with `:first` and
# the reducer returns `{:acc, a}`, so the declared accumulator is `:first |
# {:acc, a}` and the seed is a member of it. The stdout expectation holds on all
# three paths; `expected.diagnostics` carries one library warning.

# The `run` budget matches `interp`'s because this program compiles 259
# executables, and `run` starts its clock at execution-ready, so JIT lowering of
# all of them sits inside the measured window: `fz2 run` takes 3.1-3.9s here
# against a 3s default. `build` needs no override -- `fz2 build` itself is
# untimed and only the produced binary's execution is measured.
#
# THE COMMENT BLOCK ABOVE THE BLANK LINE IS 17 LINES AND THE DIAGNOSTICS GOLDEN
# DEPENDS ON THAT COUNT. `fixture_matrix`'s `normalize_gutter_line_ref`
# subtracts a fixture's leading-comment-line count from EVERY gutter number it
# renumbers, including one rendered from `runtime:Enum.fz`, so
# `expected.diagnostics` stores `250 |` for the line `fz2 interp` renders as
# `267 |`. Prose that needs to grow goes HERE, below the blank line where the
# normaliser's `take_while` has already stopped. fz-kdt.19 owns the defect.

fn main() do
  xs = [1, 2, 3, 4]
  range = 1..7//2
  map = %{2 => :two, 1 => :one}

  # reduce/2 across List, Range, and Map
  dbg(Enum.reduce(xs, fn (x, acc) -> x * acc end))
  dbg(Enum.reduce(range, fn (x, acc) -> x * acc end))
  dbg(Enum.reduce(map, fn ({k, _v}, {ak, av}) -> {ak + k, av} end))
  # reduce/3 across List, Range, and Map
  dbg(Enum.reduce(xs, 0, fn (x, acc) -> acc + x end))
  dbg(Enum.reduce(range, 0, fn (x, acc) -> acc + x end))
  dbg(Enum.reduce(map, 0, fn ({k, _v}, acc) -> acc + k end))
  # reduce_while/3 across List, Range, and Map
  dbg(Enum.reduce_while(xs, 0, fn (x, acc) ->
    if x < 3 do
      {:cont, acc + x}
    else
      {:halt, acc}
    end
  end))
  dbg(Enum.reduce_while(range, 0, fn (x, acc) ->
    if x < 5 do
      {:cont, acc + x}
    else
      {:halt, acc}
    end
  end))
  dbg(Enum.reduce_while(map, [], fn ({k, v}, acc) ->
    if k < 2 do
      {:cont, [v | acc]}
    else
      {:halt, acc}
    end
  end))
  dbg(Enum.each([:a, :b], fn (x) -> x end))
  dbg(Enum.count(range))
  dbg(Enum.count(xs, fn (x) -> x > 2 end))
  dbg(Enum.member?(range, 5))
  dbg(Enum.member?(range, 6))
  dbg(Enum.member?(map, {1, :one}))
  dbg(Enum.to_list(range))
  dbg(Enum.to_list(map))
  dbg(Enum.reverse(xs))
  dbg(Enum.reverse(range, [:tail]))
end
